    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29456" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mōlĭo</span></b> , īre,
		4 (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>act.</i> collat. form of molior). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To build, erect</i> (post-Aug.): neque quis quid
			molit, S. C. ap. <i><span class="en">Front. Aquaed. 129</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In a <i>pass.</i> signif., <i>to set in motion,
			start</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jam sospitatricis deae peculiaris pompa
					moliebatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 11, p. 261, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
